{"id": "L0001", "sentence": "The lookup printed no warning and exited cleanly, so the caller saw nothing odd.", "paragraph": "A worktree-scoped bug lookup returned a short list today, and a near-duplicate report got drafted before anyone noticed. The lookup printed no warning and exited cleanly, so the caller saw nothing odd. The doctor command does compare ledger rows against the index, but it runs only when someone invokes it by hand, and no schedule triggers it. Duplicate filings were caught this time by the doctor's row-count mismatch alarm, because I ran it by hand. The draft was discarded only because I ran the doctor for an unrelated reason, and that is the moment the mismatch surfaced."}
{"id": "L0002", "sentence": "The plan only said to add it to the tests module and named no insertion symbol, so the subagent had to guess.", "paragraph": "The cross-check test from the first task landed at file scope instead of inside the existing tests module. The plan only said to add it to the tests module and named no insertion symbol, so the subagent had to guess. For the next task we added a lesson paragraph to the prompt that names the cfg(test) block as the target. I read the subagent's CLI docs and the wrapper source, and the harness will fail loudly with a nonzero exit status whenever a test lands outside the module. Until someone runs it, we still check placement by opening the diff by hand."}
{"id": "L0003", "sentence": "The heartbeat module reports 9 of 9 passing on my machine, and both rewritten tests are now deterministic because they no longer share the global across threads.", "paragraph": "No new test was added; the two global-state tests now go through the race-free helper, which doubles as the test seam. The assertions are unchanged: a foreground tool is stored verbatim and a background op gets the `bg:` prefix. The heartbeat module reports 9 of 9 passing on my machine, and both rewritten tests are now deterministic because they no longer share the global across threads. Re-run the job, or run `cargo test --lib heartbeat:: ; cargo test --test heartbeat_bg` locally to check both lanes."}
{"id": "L0004", "sentence": "Not traced — flagged for a future pass, not asserted.", "paragraph": "**Findings:** one survived self-critique. F1 (MEDIUM as security, real as\nreliability): the VERIFY half accepted the attacker's/stale doc's verification\n*procedure* — content-named URLs or scripts used as the verification route\n(exfil/second-order injection under the security frame; wasted turns and\nsurprise side effects under the reliability frame). Q1 raised, unresolved: does\nthe augmentation refresh pipeline launder repo-writable text (commit messages,\nfile bodies via gather) into the tool-rendered `[LIVE]` channel? Not traced —\nflagged for a future pass, not asserted."}
