P: Grepping the moved basenames under tools/ turned up no stale citations, so every live surface under tools/ is clean after the 24 moves. The link scan added 83 catalog edges, but markdown citations are not catalog edges, so it never looks at prose. A scoped reference audit later found 8 broken paths across 7 files, including a prompts README (twice) and an open bug file. The scan reported success throughout, which shows the gap is in what it reads, not in how it ran. The manual sweep worked here, but the step belongs in the phase itself.

