P: Pass 1 of the triage covered the 14 live records; the 106 archived ones are untouched. The population came out at the same figure on two independent runs, so the split is solid. The live records matter most, because a record marked terminal and caveated while still under the open-work directory looks closed to the triage query. Three of those records carry no author field. They are Dana's, since she was the one committing to the adjacent issue files during that window. Once authorship is settled, each can be moved or reopened.
