L0292 S: I wrote a test asserting that equal shas mean the same build, and it went red when two builds, one from a dirty tree, shared a sha. 
P: The doc comment holds for the mismatch direction: a sidecar stamped with sha A, read by a binary built at sha B, is rejected, and the test for that passes on every platform we run. The gap is the converse. I wrote a test asserting that equal shas mean the same build, and it went red when two builds, one from a dirty tree, shared a sha. I then reworded the assertion to require equal shas plus a clean-tree flag. The red from the equal-sha assertion carries over to the dirty-flag assertion, so the guard is known to reject dirty builds.
