L0300 S: The wine job reports a zero parent pid because the snapshot call returns an invalid handle there; the log line from run 5512 shows the early return. 
P: The wine job reports a zero parent pid because the snapshot call returns an invalid handle there; the log line from run 5512 shows the early return. The test was called `ppid_nonzero_all_lanes` until last month, when it was split by platform. On unix the assertion holds, since getppid is a plain syscall and returns the launching shell's pid. The windows sibling asserts zero, which matches what the wine lane returns.
L0301 S: What changed was a timing measurement: isolating the mutation cost 87 s the first time and 11 s per run after that, which is faster than using the shared tree. 
P: The mutation probe was built on 2026-09-14, and it replaced the marker design we had argued over for two weeks. What changed was a timing measurement: isolating the mutation cost 87 s the first time and 11 s per run after that, which is faster than using the shared tree. The option we had ranked second because we assumed it was expensive therefore became the default. The script exits zero on every mutant it is given, so it runs to completion without crashing on any of them. Isolation is built into the script itself, so a mutant cannot leak into the working tree.
L0302 S: The gate itself was added by codescout-0a, because the blame for the `notice_once` lines shows that agent as the author. 
