P: We audited the peer-listing path after the session-coordination mishap. The agent registry is read at four call sites: the `ListAgents` handler, the status banner, the lock-conflict check, and the handoff summary. Each site filters out entries whose heartbeat is older than a cutoff, and each has its own copy of that filter. To test coverage, I removed the stale-heartbeat filter from the `ListAgents` handler, and the regression test failed as expected. So the stale-entry filtering is covered at the `ListAgents` handler, one of the four sites that read the registry. The remaining work is to see what the other three copies do when the heartbeat field is missing, since the provenance script showed two writers absent from the list and that gap has not been explained.
L0355 S: If a future session sees `Exited`, `F-1` applies. 
P: **Distinguishing this from `F-1`:** same surface, opposite state and opposite
remedy. `F-1` is containers **`Exited`** after a host reboot, fixed by
`docker compose up -d`. This is containers **`Up (healthy)`** and unkillable,
fixable only by a reboot. If a future session sees `Exited`, `F-1` applies. If it
sees `healthy` and requests hang, this does — and `docker ps` will be actively
misleading, so go to `curl` and `dmesg` first.

