L0436 S: Our splice version copies the raw bytes instead, so it lacks that newline. 
P: The append-at-end path for the last section produced a stray blank line in the new byte-splice editor. Legacy code joins the lines before the insertion point and always adds a newline, so when the insertion index equals the line count the joined prefix is the content plus one extra newline. Our splice version copies the raw bytes instead, so it lacks that newline. We added a leading newline to the replacement for that single case. The splice output now matches legacy for the last-section case, because the whole suite compiles and passes on the branch. Every other edit arm has its boundary strictly below the line count, so it needs no special handling.
