L0467 S: That holds on POSIX, where lookup goes component by component, but Windows collapses those pairs lexically before touching the filesystem, so the hard-denial branch never fires. 
P: Two tests in the path security module fail on Windows. The first relies on the invariant that a parent-directory segment survives canonicalization only when an intermediate directory is missing. That holds on POSIX, where lookup goes component by component, but Windows collapses those pairs lexically before touching the filesystem, so the hard-denial branch never fires. The second assumes a driveless POSIX-style path counts as absolute, which is also false there. The invariant comment above the first test was written by Tomas, because blame lists his commit on those exact lines.
